      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Overall package from Zip was well priced. Picked up a 10kw system with 20kw battery and two of the house circuits on power out back up for similar price to quotes received through SolarQuotes. Previous experience with follow up issues has made us not believe the dearer installers are necessarily going to help out down the track, though I think they are more likely to if they are mentioned favourably on SolarQuotes.20kw battery isn't sufficient for us. We knew this. It will dramatically reduce our bill though. Our self sufficiency was running above 90% but a couple of big trips has meant the EV was charging overnight and has dragged that down.Only installed about 6 weeks ago.Rough calculations indicating pay off in 3.5 to 4 years. (our calculations)Contractors were good. No problems so far with install and operation.No bullying BS form Zip before the sign up at all, which was a shock. Sorry for the pun.Cheers",
